<div class="page">
  <h2 class="section-title">Aims and Scope</h2>
  <div class="two-column-body">
    <div class="column">
      <p>Applied Marketing Analytics is the major peer-reviewed, professional journal for all those involved in measuring, managing and analysing marketing activity to maximise both effectiveness and return on investment. Guided by its respected Editorial Board, each quarterly 100-page issue publishes in-depth studies, case studies, research papers and reviews written by leading experts in the field. The journal’s target readership includes anyone with an interest in marketing analytics, customer insight and business intelligence, but specifically senior marketing professionals based at brand owners, marketing analytics consultants, advertising agencies, media service providers, market researchers and consumers researchers as well as academics and researchers in universities and business schools.</p>
      <p><strong>Applied Marketing Analytics</strong>, published both in print and online, seeks to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Explore the practical strategies, technologies and techniques used in the application of marketing analytics as well as a identifying emerging industry trends, best practice lessons and case studies.</li>
        <li>Publish quantitative and qualitative research, policy reviews, book reviews, and legal and regulatory briefings of direct relevance to the practice of marketing analytics.</li>
        <li>Publish leading authors in the field and a wide range of contemporary research on the financial service, hospitality, media and entertainment, healthcare, consumer and business brands, social media, and not-for-profit sectors.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The journal’s scope is international and includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Accountability, measurement and performance benchmarks in marketing.</li>
        <li>Aligning marketing metrics with business goals.</li>
        <li>Attribution of digital and social media effects.</li>
        <li>Big data analytics.</li>
        <li>Business intelligence and customer insight.</li>
        <li>The new customer decision journey and the role of analytics.</li>
        <li>The value of social media to understand consumer behaviour.</li>
        <li>Customer relationship management, segmentation, behaviour and engagement.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <ul>
        <li>Optimizing marketing value, retention and loyalty.</li>
        <li>Corporate data governance and corporate analytics business structure.</li>
        <li>Compliance and regulation, including international privacy policies.</li>
        <li>Data mining, warehousing, affinity analysis, predictive analytics and machine learning.</li>
        <li>Online and offline marketing channels, cross channel analytics and marketing mix analysis.</li>
        <li>Using analytics to inform content and marketing decisions.</li>
        <li>New technologies in marketing analytics.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h3 class="section-title">SUBMISSIONS AND SUBSCRIPTIONS</h3>
